JSON-to-Directory Souffle.

A light, airy souffle that rises from a JSON document into a whole tree of directories, files, symbolic links and executable scripts. The batter is the document itself, taken from the refrigerator one byte (as a decimal number) at a time; it is checked for UTF-8 and JSON lumps, every name is inspected, and only then is the shell script that builds the tree folded together, liquefied and poured into the baking dish. A spoiled batter yields only a note from the chef. Generated by gen/chef.py from json2dir.stk; Acme::Chef reads it.

